   "evidence": "`def openHomEquiv ... := ContinuousLinearEquiv.arrowCongr (ContinuousLinearEquiv.refl \u211d _) (openEquiv x)`. A grep for a comparison between the pullback of a Hom bundle and the Hom of pullbacks finds nothing in `TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/VectorBundle/{Pullback,Hom}.lean` or Mathlib `Geometry/Manifold/VectorBundle`. The same shape appears at `Quotient/BundleMap.lean:74` (`c *\u1d56 (fun q \u21a6 V q \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] W q)`) and `LieAlgebroid/Restrict.lean:192`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/VectorBundle/Density/OpenSubset.lean",
   "fix": "Prove a general result first. For a continuous `c : C(B', B)` and bundles `V`, `W` on `B`, give the fibrewise equivalence `Hom(c*V, c*W) \u2243 c*Hom(V, W)` and its smooth total-space map (diffeomorphism), placed in `VectorBundle/Pullback.lean` or `Hom.lean`. Then derive `openHomEquiv`/`openHomDiffeomorph` by composing it with post-composition by `openEquiv`/`openDiffeomorph` on the target. This removes the ad-hoc frame proof.",
   "issue": "`openHomEquiv` is `arrowCongr refl (openEquiv x)` and has nothing density-specific in it, yet the PR proves its smoothness only for target `DensityBundle`. `eventually_trivializationAt_openHomEquiv_eq` (~50 lines of `inCoordinates`/`symm_pullback`/`erw`/`change`) re-derives the general Hom-of-pullback frame comparison and then repeats the density frame argument.",
   "line": 168
  }
